1. Executive Summary

The Agentic SDLC Automation Platform is an AI-assisted engineering solution designed to automate the end-to-end development lifecycle of data pipelines on Google Cloud Platform.

The platform uses specialized AI agents to interpret mapping documents, generate database DDLs, create and configure tables, develop Dataflow pipelines, package Dataflow Flex Templates, generate Airflow DAGs, implement Silver-layer SQL transformations, execute automated validations, and prepare controlled deployments.

The solution supports enterprise data ingestion from SQL Server, Oracle, REST APIs, files, and Confluent Kafka. Data is ingested into the Bronze layer using Dataflow, with Cloud Composer coordinating pipeline execution and dependencies. Silver-layer transformations follow the approved mapping sheet and are executed through Airflow DAGs. The Gold layer contains business-ready data for downstream analytics and reporting.

A centralized engineering workbench provides visibility into agent activities, generated artifacts, test results, deployment approvals, and operational health.

The architecture combines AI-assisted development with deterministic execution, automated testing, infrastructure as code, controlled CI/CD, and enterprise security.

Primary objective: Transform mapping-driven data engineering into a standardized, repeatable, and governed automated lifecycle—from requirements to production deployment.

2. Business and Technical Objectives

* Automate DDL generation and table creation.
* Generate Dataflow batch and streaming pipelines using standardized templates.
* Automate Dataflow Flex Template packaging, publishing, and version management.
* Generate and maintain Cloud Composer Airflow DAGs.
* Generate Silver SQL from approved mapping sheets.
* Automate unit testing, integration testing, schema validation, and data reconciliation.
* Standardize Git workflows, code reviews, CI/CD, and environment promotion.
* Provide AI-assisted failure analysis and controlled remediation proposals.
* Improve engineering productivity, consistency, traceability, and operational visibility.
* Enforce security, least-privilege access, governance, and human approval controls.

