12. Implementation Roadmap

Phase 1 — Platform Foundation

Establish the repository, mapping specification, backend workflow manager, engineering workbench, agent runtime, and security boundaries.

Phase 2 — DDL and Silver SQL Automation

Generate DDL, table definitions, mapping-driven Silver SQL, and Airflow DAGs. Validate the complete workflow on a representative table.

Phase 3 — Dataflow Flex Template Automation

Generate Dataflow pipeline code, build container images, publish Flex Templates, and execute controlled development jobs.

Phase 4 — End-to-End Integration

Connect source ingestion to Bronze, Bronze to Silver, and Silver to Gold. Add integration tests, reconciliation, dependency management, and backfill support.

Phase 5 — Enterprise Production Readiness

Implement protected releases, production approval gates, immutable artifact promotion, centralized monitoring, audit reporting, and controlled remediation.

13. Key Design Decisions Before Implementation

The following must be finalized before production development:

1. Iceberg catalog and the supported read/write integration.
2. Source extraction strategy for SQL Server and Oracle.
3. Approved mapping-sheet format and canonical pipeline specification.
4. Dataflow Flex Template language, dependency management, and image lifecycle.
5. Standard Airflow DAG templates and execution conventions.
6. SQL execution engine and supported Silver-layer DDL/DML.
7. Development, QA, and production project boundaries.
8. Agent tool permissions, model configuration, and workflow-state persistence.
9. Security, audit retention, data governance, and approval requirements.

14. Target-State Outcome

The platform will establish a standardized engineering lifecycle:

Mapping Sheet → Metadata Specification → DDL and Table Creation → Dataflow Pipeline Generation → Flex Template Build and Publication → Airflow DAG Generation → Silver SQL Generation → Automated Testing → Git Review → CI/CD → Approved Deployment → Runtime Monitoring and Audit

The outcome is a governed, scalable, and reusable automation platform that reduces manual development effort while preserving reliable data processing, security, reproducibility, and human control over production changes.